course: dictionary
lesson: 2989
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number, and the context tells you which one to choose. Read the sentence around the word first, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Players waiting to bat stand behind the fence or in the dugout (the team's low shelter beside the field).» The words bat, fence and field tell you this is about sport, so a dugout is the low shelter where the team sits.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. A dugout canoe is a boat, so it would make no sense beside a sports field. Only one meaning fits each time.
fact: A dugout can be a canoe made by hollowing out a tree trunk.
fact: A dugout can be a shelter dug in the ground, used by soldiers in war.
fact: In sports, a dugout is the low covered bench area where players and coaches sit.
fact: «Dugout canoe» is the phrase for the boat, and «in the dugout» is the phrase for the sports bench.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word, and the context shows you which meaning to use.
exercise: In history, people made a «dugout canoe» from one tree. What is a dugout canoe? | *A canoe made by hollowing out a tree trunk | A bench where players sit | A shelter dug in the ground | A kind of sports ground
exercise: «Players waiting to bat stand behind the fence or in the dugout.» Find and copy the word that tells you this is about sport. | or | Players | behind | *bat
exercise: «Players waiting to bat stand behind the fence or in the dugout.» What does dugout mean here? | *The low covered bench where the team sits | A canoe made from a tree trunk | A wooden fence | A hole where soldiers hide from enemy fire
test: «Soldiers sheltered in a dugout, deep under the ground.» What does dugout mean here? | A kind of sports ground | *A shelter dug in the ground | A canoe made from a tree trunk | A bench where players sit
test: «The coach shouted instructions from the dugout.» Which meaning fits? | A trunk of a tree | A canoe made by hollowing out a tree | *A low covered bench where coaches sit | A shelter dug in the ground for soldiers
exam: Ben says «in the dugout» means a boat in a sports match. What is the best answer? | No, a dugout is a shop | Yes, in sport a dugout is a canoe | Yes, a dugout is always a boat | *No, in sport a dugout is the low covered bench where players and coaches sit
